 ## Background
-Logarithmic Depth Partitioning, also referred to as Voxelization Layer Distribution, was introduced in the context of memory-efficient on-the-fly voxelization of particle data [S1]. It addresses the need for continuous appearance in rendered boundary surfaces by enforcing minimum angle resolution during voxelization [S1]. The method is particularly relevant for SPH (Smoothed Particle Hydrodynamics) simulations and other particle-based rendering techniques where surface extraction from voxelized data is required [S1].
